Package: TransSynPALM
Title: Transfer Learning with Synthetic Phenotype Assisted Linear Mixed Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Haoyu", "Yang", email = "haoyuyang@hsph.harvard.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ruoyu", "Wang", role = "aut"),
    person("Xihong", "Lin", email = "xlin@hsph.harvard.edu", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Genome-wide association testing in an under-represented target
    population whose phenotype is measured in only a fraction of participants.
    TransSynPALM fits two synthetic phenotype assisted linear mixed models
    (Syn-PALM), one on the target population and one on the pooled
    target-plus-source cohort. Unphenotyped participants enter through a
    machine-learning synthetic phenotype used as a control variate. The pooled
    estimator is decorrelated from the target-only one through their joint
    family-level sandwich covariance. The two resulting p-values are combined
    under a four-group composite null, so source-specific associations are not
    reported as target associations.
